6,"Karen, Paku in Myanmar (Burma) people group profile | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/14268/BM,"Most Paku Karen also speak S'gaw Karen or Burmese, and because their language has never had a written form, they have long used S'gaw Karen literature. Taungoo District, where most Paku people live, has a long history.Sino-Tibetan. Glottolog Language Family.","Karen, Paku",Sino-Tibetan
